Negative control for the rail never exporting its own width (`AC2.4` · `R6-7`).

Drops the stop's `min-w-0` and leaves the rest — the rail still takes the page's
width, still draws every stop, still seeks. So the only claim that can go red is
the ruled one: a stop's label wraps INSIDE its own column. A flex item defaults
to `min-width:auto` and refuses to go below its content, so one long Gherkin
sentence sets the row's minimum, the page shell sizes itself to it, and the
canvas gains the horizontal scrollbar the rail is supposed to absorb.

Re-targeted 2026-08-13: under `R7-8` the rail is its own full-width row, so the
mechanism that keeps it inside the page moved from the lane's `w-0 flex-1` basis
to the stop's own `min-w-0`. Same claim, same red, current mechanism.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the scene-rail width case — the rail's stops are shrinkable, so the row
cannot report a long scene as the page's minimum width.

